    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0201" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1953a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Substance]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-02-04T23:00:00-05:00">February 4, 1941—11
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>80. Reference is made to your No. 126 of January 27, 7 p.m., final sentence in
                    paragraph No. 1. Assuming that you lack an official text, the Department would
                    be interested in a close comparison by the Embassy of available press reports in
                    order to determine whether Minister Matsuoka indicated that the attackers at
                    Marco Polo Bridge were the Japanese.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
